::Q1::Which command is used to add FastAPI with its standard dependencies to a project managed by uv?
{
~pip install fastapi uvicorn
=uv add "fastapi[standard]"
~uv install fastapi
~uv add fastapi-cli-only
}

::Q2::Which command starts a FastAPI application in development mode when using uv?
{
~uv run fastapi production
=uv run fastapi dev
~uv run fastapi start --production
~uv run pytest fastapi
}

::Q3::In a FastAPI route defined with a path like "/products/\{product_id\}", where the function argument product_id is typed as an integer and is not read from the query string or the request body, what type of parameter is product_id?
{
~A query parameter
=A path parameter
~A request-body parameter
~An HTTP header
}

::Q4::In a Pydantic model, a numeric field is declared as a float with a validation rule requiring the value to be strictly greater than zero. What does this constraint enforce?
{
~The value must be zero or greater
=The value must be greater than zero
~The value must be an integer
~The value must be less than zero
}

::Q5::In a FastAPI route, a parameter is set to specify the Pydantic model that describes the shape of the response data. What is the purpose of this parameter?
{
~It determines which HTTP method the route accepts
=It controls the declared shape of the response and helps prevent unintended fields from being returned
~It starts the Uvicorn server
~It determines which database table is queried
}

::Q6::What role does Uvicorn play in a FastAPI application?
{
~It is the Pydantic validation library
~It is the OpenAPI documentation format
=It is an ASGI server that can run the FastAPI application
~It is the database layer used by FastAPI
}